1. Definitions
--------------

1.1. "Ethos" 
    means the distinctive guiding principles, style, intent, and/or cultural or 
    philosophical positioning embodied by the Work (including how the Work 
    frames its purpose, conventions, and audience-facing messaging).

1.2. "Work" 
    means the original work covered by this License and all files included with 
    it at the time of distribution.

1.3. "Derivative Work" 
    means any work that is based upon, recasts, transforms, or adapts the Work.
    Examples include adding, deleting or modifying source code.

1.4. "Incorporation" 
    means any inclusion, reuse, embedding, or combination of portions of the 
    Work into another software item.
    Examples include using the Work as an implementation dependency, bundling 
    portions of the Work, or building a software item using a language, 
    framework, or library derived from the Work.

1.5. "Meaningfully Inspired" 
    means any work for which the author reasonably drew on ideas, structure, 
    naming conventions, architecture, implementation patterns or ethos from the 
    Work such that a knowledgeable person could recognize influence from the 
    Work, even if code is not directly copied.

1.6. "Software Item" 
    means any program, script, library, data format, model, or other 
    computational artifact.


